---
description: Apply strict, maintainable TypeScript quality rules.
globs: "**/*.ts"
alwaysApply: false
---

- Preserve strict typing; avoid `any`, unchecked casts, and non-null assertions without evidence.
- Prefer small cohesive functions, explicit dependencies, and domain-oriented names.
- Model expected failures explicitly and preserve error causes.
- Keep business behavior deterministic and testable.
- Do not silence compiler, linter, or runtime errors to make a check pass.
- Avoid placeholder code and premature abstractions.
